                  <handDesc>
                     <handNote xml:id="h1" script="Ethiopic">
                        <seg type="script">Eighteenth-century script</seg>
                        <desc>Fine and regular handwriting. The scribe <persName role="scribe" ref="https://betamasaheft.eu/PRS15281GabraMik">Gabra Mikāʾel</persName> is
                           mentioned in <ref target="#coloph1"/> and in several supplication formulas 
                           (e.g. <locus target="#62rb #65ra"/>). The handwriting is characterized by uniform, rounded, curved and less spaced letters. 
                           Some distinctive features: The words <foreign xml:lang="gez">እግዚአብሔር፡</foreign> and 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">እግዚእ፡</foreign> are written several times with ligatures of 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">ግ</foreign> and <foreign xml:lang="gez">ዚ</foreign> 
                           (e.g. <locus target="#44va #50ra #50rb #51rb"/>). 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">፪</foreign> is sometimes written with its loop at the bottom not closed 
                           (e.g. <locus target="#7va #53rb"/>).
                           The upper horizontal strokes of <foreign xml:lang="gez">መ</foreign>, <foreign xml:lang="gez">ሠ</foreign> and
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">ወ</foreign> (esp. <foreign xml:lang="gez">መ</foreign>) in the 1st order, are slightly slanted 
                           to the left. The sign <foreign xml:lang="gez">፤</foreign> is used a few times after the sign 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">፨</foreign> (e.g., <locus target="#49rb #57ra #65ra"/>.</desc>
                        <seg type="ink">Black; red (strong vermillion)</seg>
                        <date notBefore="1700" notAfter="1799" cert="medium">Possibly 18th century</date>
                        <list type="abbreviations">
                           <item>
                              <abbr>ዓለ፡ አሜ፡/ ዓለ፡ አ፡</abbr> for <expan>ዓለም፡ አሜን፡ </expan> (e.g. <locus target="#45vb #47ra"/>)</item>
                           <item>
                              <abbr>ለዓ፡ ዓለ፡ አሜን፡/ለዓለ፡ ዓለ፡ አሜን፡</abbr> for <expan>ለዓለመ፡ ዓለም፡ አሜን፡</expan> (e.g. <locus target="#57ra #60va"/>)</item>
                           <item>
                              <abbr>ሰላ፡</abbr> for <expan>ሰላም፡ </expan> (<locus from="62ra" to="64vb"/>, <ref target="#ms_i1.6"/>)</item>
                        </list>
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; the name of the protagonist; 
                           the donor, her relatives and the scribe; a few lines in groups
                           of two alternating with black lines on the opening pages;
                           number of each miracle; a few lines in some paragraphs; the Trinitarian
                           formula; the word <foreign xml:lang="gez">salām</foreign> and its abbreviation; elements of
                           quire marks; elements of the Ethiopic numerals; elements of the
                           punctuation marks.</seg>
                     </handNote>
                  </handDesc>
